      "dcterms:title": "On the Gram determinants of the Specht modules",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "Hoyer, Linda"
      ],
      "dcterms:issued": "D:20241107",
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2411.04021",
      "dcterms:abstract": "For every partition λ of a positive integer n, let Sλ be the corresponding Specht module of the symmetric group Sn, and let det(λ) ∈Z denote the Gram determinant of the canonical bilinear form with respect to the standard basis of Sλ. Writing det(λ) = m · 2a(2) λ for integers a(2) λ and m with m odd, we show that if the dimension of Sλ is even, then a(2) λ is also even. This confirms a conjecture posed by Richard Parker in the special case of the symmetric groups.",
      "dcterms:source": "library/arxiv-2411.04021v1/manifest.jsonld",
      "dcterms:hasVersion": "library/arxiv-2411.04021v1"
    }
  ]
